    --- - `numPoints`: The number of anchor points for the region. Returns `0` if there are no points.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_GetNumPoints)
    function GetNumPoints(): number
    --- Returns an anchor point for the region.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `anchorIndex`: Index between 1 and GetNumPoints.
    --- - `resolveCollapsed`: See SetCollapsesLayout.
    ---
    --- **Returns**
    --- - `point`: Point on this region at which it is anchored to another.
    --- - `relativeTo`: Reference to the other region to which this region is anchored.
    --- - `relativePoint`: Point on the other region to which this region is anchored.
    --- - `offsetX`: Offset right (negative for left).
    --- - `offsetY`: Offset up (negative for down).
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_GetPoint)
    function GetPoint(anchorIndex: number?, resolveCollapsed: boolean?): (FramePoint, ScriptRegion, FramePoint, uiUnit, uiUnit)
    --- Returns an anchor point by name for the region.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_GetPointByName)
    function GetPointByName(point: FramePoint, resolveCollapsed: boolean?): (FramePoint, ScriptRegion, FramePoint, uiUnit, uiUnit)
    --- Positions the region the same as another region.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `relativeTo`: The reference or name of a region.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetAllPoints)
    function SetAllPoints(relativeTo: ScriptRegion?, doResize: boolean?)
    --- Sets the region's height.
    ---
    --- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetHeight)
    function SetHeight(height: uiUnit)
    --- Sets an anchor point for the region.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `point`: FramePoint - The point of this region.
    --- - `relativeTo`: The reference or name of the other region. For example `UIParent` or `"UIParent"`.
    --- - `relativePoint`: FramePoint - The point of the other region to anchor to. If omitted, defaults to `point`.
    --- - `offsetX`: Offset right (negative for left). Requires `offsetY` to be specified.
    --- - `offsetY`: Offset up (negative for down). Requires `offsetX` to be specified.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetPoint)
    function SetPoint(point: FramePoint, relativeTo: unknown?, relativePoint: FramePoint?, offsetX: uiUnit?, offsetY: uiUnit?)
    function SetPoint(point: FramePoint, relativeTo: unknown?, ofsx: number?, ofsy: number?)
    function SetPoint(point: FramePoint, ofsx: number?, ofsy: number?)
    --- Sets the x and y offsets of all of the region's anchor points.
    ---
    --- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetPointsOffset)
    function SetPointsOffset(x: uiUnit, y: uiUnit)
    --- Sets the width and height of the region.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `width`: The width of the region.
    --- - `height`: The height of the region.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetSize)
    function SetSize(x: uiUnit, y: uiUnit)
    --- Sets the region's width.
    ---
    --- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_ScriptRegionResizing_SetWidth)
    function SetWidth(width: uiUnit)
end

